# AsyncSequence, not Combine

Rationale: [ADR-0001](../../docs/adr/0001-asyncsequence-not-combine.md).

App-owned streams use `AsyncSequence` / `AsyncStream`. Do not `import Combine` or expose Combine types. Do not copy Combine metric wiring from Biker.

```swift
// ✅ GOOD
protocol SpeedSource {
    var speeds: some AsyncSequence<Measurement<UnitSpeed>, Never> { get }
}

// ❌ BAD
import Combine
protocol SpeedSource {
    var speeds: AnyPublisher<Measurement<UnitSpeed>, Never> { get }
}
```

Forbidden in this app’s modules: `Publisher`, `AnyPublisher`, `Subject` / `PassthroughSubject` / `CurrentValueSubject`, `@Published`.

UI latest values live on Observation (`@Observable`) view models, not Combine subjects.

**Boundary exception only:** if a vendor API is Combine-only, adapt at the edge (`publisher.values` or `AsyncStream`). Combine types must not appear in this app’s public or package APIs.

When merge / combineLatest / throttle are first needed, add swift-async-algorithms — do not add Combine instead.
